feedback.body:
@bkryu  @lucifer1004  — small update on context: vLLM #54566 (DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp) now has a human approval and upstream CI running. Independent SM120 testing on that branch confirms stock FlashInfer fails on the first image request at exactly the H=32, topk=512, extra_topk=512, PBS=64 envelope added here; text-only serving works.
This PR is just 2 files / +20−10 and adds that exact tested dispatch + regression. Since #4802 overlaps the planner/launcher, could you advise whether you’d prefer this merged directly or the envelope folded into #4802?

My #4842  PR is a bit of a similar story and I’m just trying to understand if you’d rather have it all merged into #4802 first, or approve the smaller PRs first. Thanks! And hopefully I’m not being annoying, just trying to help!

Follow-up: I applied that suggested change directly to `541f378` and re-ran the full TP=2 serve (same box, same vLLM #54566 build). **It fixes it** — first image request succeeds, zero `Unsupported sparse-MLA` in the logs, vision output correct, and throughput matches the patch we'd been running all day (169 tok/s single-stream, 1051 tok/s at concurrency 16, dspark k=3, 1M max-model-len).

The exact change, in case it saves a round-trip (verbatim from my test — take or rework freely):

```diff
-  if (num_heads == 32 && topk == 512 && topk_extra == 512 && extra_page_block_size == 64) {
-    DISPATCH_DUAL_MG_CM(BF16, 32, 512, 64, 2);
-    return true;
-  }
-  if (num_heads == 64 && topk == 512 && topk_extra == 512 && extra_page_block_size == 64) {
-    DISPATCH_DUAL_MG_CM(BF16, 64, 512, 64, 2);
-    return true;
-  }
+  // topk_extra is runtime (see the comment above the macro); the extra cache
+  // arrives in both enumerated page layouts (64-token and 2-token pages), so
+  // gate only on the compile-time template parameters.
+  if (topk == 512 && extra_page_block_size == 64) {
+    if (num_heads == 32) { DISPATCH_DUAL_MG_CM(BF16, 32, 512, 64, 2); return true; }
+    if (num_heads == 64) { DISPATCH_DUAL_MG_CM(BF16, 64, 512, 64, 2); return true; }
+  }
+  if (topk == 512 && extra_page_block_size == 2) {
+    if (num_heads == 32) { DISPATCH_DUAL_MG_CM(BF16, 32, 512, 2, 2); return true; }
+    if (num_heads == 64) { DISPATCH_DUAL_MG_CM(BF16, 64, 512, 2, 2); return true; }
+  }
```

@jagat-primitive-org this should cover your TP=1 / H=64 shape too — the `(128, 2)` layout goes through the new `PBSX=2` arm with runtime `topk_extra`.

Reproduced on two DGX Spark (GB10, sm_121) nodes with this PR applied, and found a second dispatch shape the Vision variant needs on the same branch.

**Setup.** `vllm/vllm-openai:deepseekv4-flash-vision-arm64-cu130` (Docker Hub, 2026-09-01, `sha256:8568b4bb…`, vLLM `0.28.1rc1.dev137+g5ab628dd1` from the `dsv4-vision` branch, FlashInfer `0.6.18+cu130`), `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-Vision-Exp`, TP2 across the two nodes over RoCE, `--kv-cache-dtype fp8 --block-size 256 --enable-expert-parallel`. The PR's `sparse_mla_sm120_prefill.cu` was applied over the wheel's copy and the prebuilt `flashinfer_jit_cache/.../sparse_mla_sm120.so` removed so the module JIT-compiles from source (worth a note in the PR description: with the AOT artifact present, `JitSpec.is_aot` wins and a patched `.cu` is silently ignored).

**Result with only this PR's arm.** Startup gets past the compress-4 layers and then fails in the profiling pass on the compress-128 layers:

```
Unsupported sparse-MLA prefill configuration: model=DSV4 num_heads=32 topk=512 page_block_size=64 topk_extra=128 extra_page_block_size=2
```

Same widened primary top-k 512, but the compressed cache for the `compress_ratios == 128` layers is 128 wide at page block 2 (256 / 128), and `dispatch_dsv4_dual` still returns false for `topk == 512` with `extra_page_block_size == 2`.

**What made it work.** Two more arms next to the PR's, guarded the same way (`topk_extra` is a runtime argument of the non-fulltile launcher, so only the extra page size needs the template):

```cpp
if (num_heads == 32 && topk == 512 && extra_page_block_size == 2) {
  DISPATCH_DUAL_MG_CM(BF16, 32, 512, 2, 2);
  return true;
}
if (num_heads == 64 && topk == 512 && extra_page_block_size == 2) {
  DISPATCH_DUAL_MG_CM(BF16, 64, 512, 2, 2);
  return true;
}
```

With those, the model serves: 3.7k-token prompt prefill 2,079 tok/s, single-stream decode 25.3 tok/s (39.1 with DSpark k=3), prefill 2,151 tok/s at a 28k prompt, image prompts answered correctly (solid colour, shape and position). So on this vLLM branch the PR is necessary but not sufficient for the Vision checkpoint; the 512 / 128 / page-2 shape may be worth adding here or noting as a follow-up. Happy to share the full manifests if useful.
